From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 04 Oct 2026 18:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ppc64 JIT: short forward branches with veneers instead of
 10-slot padding

A forward ma_b(cond, Label*) or jump(Label*) to an unbound label used to
reserve an inverted bc plus a 10-slot trap-tagged stanza so that bind()
could patch in a load64 + mtctr + bctr if the label ended up out of the
16-bit bc range. In practice the label almost always binds in range (Ion
guards to out-of-line paths), bind() rewrote the bc short and turned all
10 slots into NOPs, and the fall-through path then executed them. Hot
Ion functions on POWER8 were 38-56% NOPs by instruction count; a
microbenchmark puts the cost at ~1.3 cycles per guard, and jumping over
the padding instead is worse (a taken branch costs more than the NOPs).

Do what the ARM64 backend does: emit the bc / b alone, keep the label-use
chain in the branch displacement field, register a deadline with the
constant-pool buffer (numShortBranchRanges = 1, veneerSize = 1) and let
it emit a veneer -- a single b in the pool island -- before the bc would
go out of range. bind() patches the bc directly when the target is in
reach, otherwise it leaves the bc pointing at its veneer and binds the
veneer. retarget() joins chains in whichever direction the link encodes.
The tagged stanza is still used by call(Label*) and the patchable
call/jump/far-jump sites, whose fixed footprints are unchanged.

Because POWER8 now gets pool islands, the places that relied on nothing
ever being inserted are fenced: haltingAlign/nopAlign no longer call
size() (which flushes everything), the wasm trap-site flushes use a new
flushPoolEntries() that empties the pool without forcing veneers, the
marked slow call and writeCodePointer sit in no-pool windows, the
out-of-line table switch is wrapped in one, and the *WithPatch helpers
take their patch offsets from the instructions they actually emit.

jit-test suite: PASSED ALL (on top of the load64-immediate patch). Two
stress tests with >32 KiB of Ion and wasm code pass under every
jit-test flag configuration. Octane 2.0 in the JS shell on POWER8, over
the load64-immediate patch: DeltaBlue 4423 -> 6334, Richards 4144 ->
5299, EarleyBoyer 12960 -> 15794, Crypto 4988 -> 5957.

Rebased onto 157.0.1 (archpower 0004/0005 backend: the maintainer already
takes the stanza offsets from the emitted instruction; trap sites now use
FaultingCodeRange/appendAndVerify, so only the pool flush changes remain).

