+//
+// Short-range branch tracking (one range): forward conditional branches to
+// unbound labels are emitted as a single `bc` whose BD field doubles as the
+// label-use chain link (see Assembler::nextLink). Each such `bc` registers a
+// deadline (range Assembler::BcRangeIdx) with the buffer; if the label is not
+// bound before the `bc` would go out of its +32 KiB reach, the buffer emits a
+// one-instruction veneer (`b`, +/-32 MiB) with the next pool and calls
+// Assembler::PatchShortRangeBranchToVeneer. Unconditional `b` branches (and
